0..76 Comment "//! The Rust extern `f(x: Option<&u32>, n: u32) -> u32` as a function row of"
77..140 Comment "//! the foreign boundary, admitted against its witness records."
141..144 Comment "//!"
145..218 Comment "//! A function type means a Hoare triple over its arguments\' and result\'s"
219..298 Comment "//! realisers. `Option<&u32>` is realised by the null niche, so `f`\'s triple is"
299..373 Comment "//! `deref_or`\'s at `u32`. Each argument\'s and the result\'s witness record"
374..447 Comment "//! summarises its realisers, read off its code by Rust\'s default layout."
448..451 Comment "//!"
452..528 Comment "//! `admit(declared, row)` compares rustc\'s printed layouts with the records"
529..609 Comment "//! clause by clause, answering `Admitted` or `Unrealised` with the first clause"
610..683 Comment "//! that fails. Each extern below differs from the row in one clause. The"
684..758 Comment "//! checker holds the layout program\'s integer comparisons as neutrals, so"
759..787 Comment "//! admission is a run here."
788..791 Comment "//!"
792..874 Comment "//! - see: `ledger/diagnostics/BoundaryUnrealised.Niche.gandr` — an extern block"
875..916 Comment "//!   refused at check time by the clause"
917..962 Comment "//!   it fails, `BoundaryUnrealised.<clause>`"
963..1042 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/interop/boundary/function-row.gandr` — the predicate"
1043..1095 Comment "//!   chosen through the layout, refused `Undecided`"
1096..1171 Comment "//! - see: `model/specification/niche-realizability.gandr` — `deref_or`\'s"
1172..1220 Comment "//!   triple and the tagged layout\'s equivalence"
1221..1300 Comment "//! - see: `library/std/src/boundary.gandr` — the row, the witness record and"
1301..1314 Comment "//!   `admit`"
1315..1382 Comment "//! - see: `library/std/src/layout.gandr` — Rust\'s default layout"
1383..1464 Comment "//! - cites: [Wagner-2024-realistic_realizability_specifying_abis_you_can_count],"
1465..1488 Comment "//!   § 3.1 and § 4.2"
1489..1492 Comment "//!"
1493..1684 Comment "//! [Wagner-2024-realistic_realizability_specifying_abis_you_can_count]: https://doi.org/10.1145/3689755 \"Wagner, Eisbach and Ahmed, Realistic Realizability: Specifying ABIs You Can Count On\""
1686..1760 Comment "// The Rust side, built by rustc 1.98.0-nightly (f28ac764c 2026-06-23) for"
1761..1832 Comment "// x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu. Its layouts are from `rustc --edition 2024"
1833..1901 Comment "// --crate-type=lib -Zprint-type-sizes` over the eight externs, with"
1902..1958 Comment "// `size_of`, `align_of` and `needs_drop` for each type:"
1959..1961 Comment "//"
1962..1989 Comment "//     #[unsafe(no_mangle)]"
1990..2050 Comment "//     pub extern \"C\" fn f(x: Option<&u32>, n: u32) -> u32 {"
2051..2098 Comment "//         match x { Some(r) => *r, None => n }"
2099..2107 Comment "//     }"
2108..2110 Comment "//"
2111..2178 Comment "//     type              size  alignment  discriminant   needs drop"
2179..2238 Comment "//     Option<&u32>      8     8          none (niche)   no"
2239..2298 Comment "//     u32               4     4          -              no"
2299..2358 Comment "//     u64               8     8          -              no"
2359..2418 Comment "//     &u32              8     8          -              no"
2419..2478 Comment "//     Tagged            16    8          -              no"
2479..2539 Comment "//     Option<Box<u32>>  8     8          none (niche)   yes"
2540..2599 Comment "//     Packed            4     1          -              no"
2600..2602 Comment "//"
2603..2681 Comment "// `Tagged` is `#[repr(C)] struct Tagged { tag: usize, ptr: *const u32 }`, the"
2682..2745 Comment "// tagged layout of `Option<&u32>` written out, and `Packed` is"
2746..2822 Comment "// `#[repr(C, packed)] struct Packed { v: u32 }`. The externs other than `f`"
2823..2895 Comment "// each differ from the row in one clause: `g` takes `n: u64`, `a` takes"
2896..2965 Comment "// `n: Packed`, `h` takes `x: &u32`, `t` takes `x: Tagged`, `b` takes"
2966..3034 Comment "// `x: Option<Box<u32>>`, `w` answers a `u64`, and `k` takes no `n`."
3036..3045 Comment "// `Nat`."
